{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts@L112","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":112,"end":116}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":112,"end":116},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:4e882ccaf9c9d993fd661310ccb527fffa92fd4521b0ce564fc7b9d4d3aaf96a","meta":{"text":"Mutable, layered matcher. Add the root `.gitignore`, then add nested `.gitignore` rules as the\nwalk descends into their directories. Layers are scoped by their `dir` prefix, so accumulating them\n(without popping) is safe — a rule from `packages/a/.gitignore` cannot leak into `packages/b/`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts@L120","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":120,"end":120}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":120,"end":120},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:0d3017dc74a00333ad1ffeecd5fb836a265721ac09dd653493cc87bae8db2e3f","meta":{"text":"Add rules scoped to `dir` (empty string for the repo root). No-op for an empty rule set."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts@L125","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":125,"end":129}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/gitignore.ts","span":{"start":125,"end":129},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:91d8098aa5f59af625b199546c2b53d6627e4eeb3607d3d7c923909a09417877","meta":{"text":"True iff `relPath` (repo-relative, POSIX) is ignored. Layers apply in insertion order (root first,\ndeeper later), and the LAST matching rule across all applicable layers wins — so a deeper\n`.gitignore` overrides a shallower one, and a `!` re-include overrides an earlier ignore."}}
